/* book Worked example: Q: A wing model has mass m = 500 kg, stiffness k = 200 kN/m and damping c = 4000 N·s/m. Find ωn, fn, ζ and the damped frequency. For a force of amplitude 1 kN, find the static deflection and the resonant amplitude.
   1. k = 200,000 N/m.
   2. ωn = √(200,000/500) = √400 = 20 rad/s; fn = 20/(2π) = 3.18 Hz.
   3. √(km) = √(200,000 × 500) = 10,000; ζ = 4000/(2 × 10,000) = 0.20, underdamped.
   4. Damped frequency: ωd = 20 × √(1 − 0.20²) = 19.60 rad/s.
   5. Static deflection: F₀/k = 1000/200,000 = 5.0 mm.
   6. At resonance: X = F₀/(2ζk) = 1000/(2 × 0.20 × 200,000) = 12.5 mm, 2.5 times the static value. Check with the general formula at r = 1: 12.5 mm; at r = 2 it falls to 1.61 mm.
   Answer: ωn = 20 rad/s, fn = 3.18 Hz, ζ = 0.20, ωd = 19.6 rad/s; static 5 mm, resonant 12.5 mm. */
