/* book Worked example 2: Q: The square plate of the earlier chapters, 800 mm × 800 mm × 4 mm with E = 70 GPa, ν = 0.30 and simply supported edges, is loaded in pure shear. Find Nxy,cr, the shear stress at buckling and the total shear force on one edge, and compare with its compressive buckling load.
   1. D = 70 × 10⁹ × 0.004³/(12 × 0.91) = 410.3 N·m.
   2. Square plate: ks = 5.35 + 4 × 1² = 9.35.
   3. Nxy,cr = 9.35 × π² × 410.3/0.8² = 59,154 N/m = 59.2 kN/m.
   4. τcr = Nxy,cr/t = 59,154/0.004 = 14.79 MPa.
   5. Edge force: Nxy,cr × 0.8 m = 47,323 N = 47.3 kN.
   6. Compression alone buckles it at 4π²D/b² = 25.3 kN/m, so the plate takes 2.34 times as much shear flow as compression before it buckles, the ratio 9.35/4.
   Answer: Nxy,cr = 59.2 kN/m, τcr = 14.79 MPa, 47.3 kN per edge; 2.34 times the compressive buckling load. */
