/* book exam traps: Using the circle Rc² + Rs² = 1 for compression with shear. The curve for a long flat panel is Rc + Rs² = 1; the circle overestimates the allowable shear. | Using kc = 4 for shear. The shear coefficient of a simply supported panel is 5.35 + 4(b/a)², 9.35 for a square. | Taking b as the longer side. In both ks and τcr, b is the shorter side of the panel. | Adding stresses in different directions, σ + τ, and comparing with one allowable. Each load is divided by its own critical value first. | Treating τcr as the collapse load of a web. A buckled web carries more shear as a tension field, if its flanges and stiffeners can take it. */
